EDICT 0009: S_Init in Host_Init on every build

Category: build-independent behaviour, no change in results (snd_null's S_Init does nothing).
On Win32 the software build's Host_Init leaves S_Init to vid_win.c, which the reference replaces (edict_vid.c), so
a Windows build with the sound of snd_dma.c (build.sh SOUND=1) never initialized it. Every build now calls S_Init
where Linux does, after R_Init: the same cvar and console order on both.

--- a/host.c
+++ b/host.c
@@ -890,7 +890,7 @@
 		Draw_Init ();
 		SCR_Init ();
 		R_Init ();
-#ifndef	_WIN32
+#if !defined(_WIN32) || defined(EDICT)	// EDICT: S_Init here on every build (patch 0009)
 	// on Win32, sound initialization has to come before video initialization, so we
 	// can put up a popup if the sound hardware is in use
 		S_Init ();
